<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Meirionnydd</h1><p class="st-meta">450 CE – 1000 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Early Welsh kingdom between the Mawddach and the Dyfi, named after a grandson of Cunedda, which gave its name to the later county of Merioneth.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>According to Welsh genealogical tradition, Meirionnydd took its name from Meirion, a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cunedda">Cunedda</a>, who was granted the land between the rivers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afon-mawddach">Mawddach</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-dyfi">Dyfi</a> in the 5th century. Like other Cunedda stories, this is a later legend, but a separate royal line for Meirionnydd is recorded in medieval genealogies.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is recorded of its government. The kingdom covered a mountainous coastal region including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cadair-idris">Cadair Idris</a>, with farming on the valley floors and the coast, and its people were linked by sea with the rest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cardigan-bay">Cardigan Bay</a>. Its kings appear to have been subordinate to the more powerful rulers of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-gwynedd">Kingdom of Gwynedd</a> for much of their history.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Meirionnydd was absorbed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-gwynedd">Kingdom of Gwynedd</a>, probably by the 10th century, becoming one of its cantrefi. After the English conquest of 1283 it formed the core of the county of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merionethshire">Merioneth</a>, and the name survives in the region of Meirionnydd today.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 450 CE – 1000 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emble